WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.180
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.830
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.280
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.780
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.680
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.880
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.880
...all are your friends

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.790
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.390
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.590
I long to fly freely

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.790
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.690
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:12.190
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:32.080
Romeo was poor, but he was raised in a warm, kind household.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.380
But then, on the day of the town festival

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.580
a man known as The God of Death came in search of children.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.880
Seeking to obtain Romeo, the God of Death

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.280
set fire to his father's sole remaining cornfield.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.780
As the festival was going on,

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.180
Romeo's cornfield was being engulfed in flames.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.480
Episode 2: Destiny's Beginnings:

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.480
The Family Within the Flames.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.580
It's one of our goats.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:19.480
Romeo!

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:26.480
It's too dangerous. Stay here.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.480
But....!

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.480
Dad!

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.480
Stay back!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.060
It's Jessica.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.580
Roberto!

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.590
Romeo!

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.680
Dad!

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:19.880
Come here!

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.880
Be careful!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.380
What are you doing?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.480
Go back!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.480
But...

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.480
Hurry up!!!

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:28.880
Hurry!!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.080
Romeo!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.380
Romeo!

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:58.780
Mom...

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:02.980
Romeo...

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.380
Jessica...

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.680
What are you thinking of doing?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:13.680
Roberto...

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.280
Roberto is still in there!

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:33.680
Roberto!

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.680
Dad!

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.080
Dear!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.080
Dad!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.480
Are you two ok?

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.280
The fire burned for three days and nights.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.880
And by the time it finally died down,

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.280
Romeo's father had lost everything.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.880
Dear...

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:10.980
How is your head?

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.980
Does it hurt?

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.780
No... Don't worry.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:17.980
Oh, good.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:25.380
But... I have to have a talk with Romeo.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.880
He still shows some carelessness.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.780
Compared with poor Roberto,

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.080
we're extremely fortunate.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.880
I feel so sorry for them.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.480
They lost everything, down to their last cornfield.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.680
How will they survive from now on?

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.980
The rumors say that

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.680
they are going deeper and deeper into debt.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.580
Look!!

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.980
It's the God of Death!

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.180
Romeo is his target.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.980
He's planning to try to buy Romeo.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.230
And we can do nothing but stand here and pity them.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:14.680
Yeah...

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.080
Selling Romeo might be

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.280
the only chance that family has to survive.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.480
And then? What did you do then?

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.780
Come on! Tell us!

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:24.780
Tell us!

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:26.280
Sure...

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.480
Come on Romeo!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.980
Stop moping around and talk.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.930
Then there was this cracking sound around me, like the snapping sound of a fire...

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:36.680
A crackling sound? Were you scared?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.480
Just a little...

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.880
But, brother rescued a goatling!

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.080
Wow!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.480
Awesome!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.280
Romeo's a real hero, eh?

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.880
I changed my mind about you, Romeo.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.380
I would have run away for sure!

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.120
Well, didn't I say so?

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.880
Romeo's a hero.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.780
The town's greatest hero, huh...

00:06:58.880 --> 00:06:59.980
Hooray!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.280
Brother's a hero!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.780
Hooray!

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.080
A hero!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.080
Hooray!

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.080
Romeo! And you little ones too!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.480
Dinner's ready!

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:09.490
OK!

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.280
Is that all?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.300
Hey now!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.280
Don't say things like that in front of Mom or Dad!

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.280
Why?

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.380
Because of the fire, we are in dire straits rights now.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.070
You gotta be tough.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:24.840
Ok, I will.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.230
I'll be tough!

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.230
Me too.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.980
All right then.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:33.130
See ya later...

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:38.780
Wait, Romeo!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.080
What about clearing the ashes away from the fire?

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.780
Clearing away the ashes...?

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.100
Your dad told you, didn't he?

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.680
Clean up the burnt field, he said.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.580
Really! You're the eldest son.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.080
What are we going to do if you can't hold things together?

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:56.580
Oh, right.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.680
Even you guys could do something like clearing away a field, right?

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.180
Yeah!

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.180
All right now, I'm leaving it to you!

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:04.680
Romeo!

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.380
If I fish up something delicious, that'll make Mom and Dad happy! Right?

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.080
Romeo, as was his nature,

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.980
tried his best, wanting to do what he could to be useful.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:52.980
Carlo!

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:56.180
Ah! Blood!

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.330
Whats wrong?

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.680
Where's Romeo?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.280
I'm back.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.280
Romeo.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:19.780
Yes

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.280
Where've you been?

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.280
The same valley as usual,

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.980
but I didn't catch a thing.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.980
I thought I told you to clear away the ashes from the fire.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.930
Well, you know, I told the little ones...

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.230
I ask you to do it!!!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.480
And it's not just the first or second time

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.180
that you haven't done as you were told.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.280
You go off by yourself and do as you please.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.880
No matter how old you get,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.080
you are still a selfish baby!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:48.980
Think about what you've done!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.380
And finish the job NOW!

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:55.980
Not a baby...

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.480
I'm not a baby!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:07.580
You don't understand!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.980
You just don't understand at all.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.380
I'm trying my best too.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.280
I saved that goat, didn't I?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.430
Everyone's praising me for it.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.830
And still...

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:29.480
Dad is still...

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.280
always angry!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.680
All you do...

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:35.980
All you do is...

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.380
just act big and get mad!

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.230
As if...

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:44.680
As if I hadn't saved a single damn goat!

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.280
Dear...

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.280
Leave him alone.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.430
Are you going out?

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.630
I was wondering where Romeo could be at this hour.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.680
Saying such things to his parents...

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.680
Let him be.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.280
Are you worried about the rumors of the God of Death?

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.080
I'm going out for a bit.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.080
Romeo!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.280
What's the matter?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.630
I ran away form home.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:02.780
RAN AWAY?!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.780
It's ok. There's no one here.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.780
This way, Romeo. We can hide here.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:19.780
Anita!

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:27.980
How fun! It feels like we're eloping!

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.880
What's eloping?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.780
A pair of lovers flee and hide, hand in hand!

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.580
Well, for one night, this will do.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:38.960
What will you do afterwards?

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.580
I don't know. But...

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.780
I'm absolutely not going back home.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.980
Is it true, that Romeo will be sold...?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.680
Yes indeed...

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.480
bought by that man called the God of Death.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.980
The whole town's buzzing with rumors.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:59.780
Roberto could't possibly do something like that,

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:02.080
to sell his own child!

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.080
But the two little brothers are a different story,

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:08.280
No matter what, I know he would't sell them.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.130
After all...

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.880
They're his real sons...

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.330
Romeo's his real son too, isn't he?

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.980
This is just between you and me...

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.280
The truth is, a long time ago I heard a strange rumor.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.280
I came to talk.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:43.680
Romeo's real parents died in the war.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.630
Roberto's not his real father.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:51.630
That's a lie!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:53.630
Romeo!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.580
That's  just a LIE!

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.780
Romeo! Wait!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.180
A lie...

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.280
It's got to be.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.980
A LIE!

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:14.180
Anita!

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.980
Ma'am...

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.680
Something terrible happened with Romeo!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.980
Is that true? That Romeo will be sold?

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:27.480
Yes, bought by the man called the God of Death. The town's just buzzing with the rumors.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:28.980
Sold?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.080
Roberto's not his real father.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.280
Not his real father...

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.280
Go away!

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.080
Mom!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.080
I've been looking for you all over.

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.680
Lets go home, Romeo.

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:54.680
I'm not...

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:56.080
I'm not Dad's son.

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.880
I'M NOT DAD'S...

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:07.880
It's true.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:16.180
I was going to tell you...

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.980
...when you were a little older.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:20.980
Mom...

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:24.680
Will I be sold?

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.880
No! How could we?

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.270
Romeo!

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:38.330
I want you to see something.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.580
I'll give you 30 francs tomorrow

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.380
and take him the day after.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.180
Our destination is Milan.

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:49.080
He'll work there cleaning chimneys.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.780
It's a simple deal.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.580
You wanted to show me something?

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:14.280
Your mom got married to Roberto

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.280
when you were just two years old.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:19.480
The wedding was in December.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:23.180
Bright white snow was falling.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.480
We had the priest come

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:29.180
and conduct a simple ceremony with just the family.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.380
Jessica... Do you think I'd be a good father?

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.380
Daddy...

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.680
Oh! He called me Daddy!

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.380
Jessica...

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:50.580
I promise I'll make our boy happy!

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:53.280
Thank you... Roberto.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.580
Daddy! Faster! Faster!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.280
Here we go, Romeo!

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.280
Open... There you go....

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.580
But then, that winter...

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.480
Daddy... Daddy...

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.580
You fell ill with severe pneumonia.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.880
Everyone had lent their every effort,

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.650
but still your health worsened daily.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:20.780
They said you were doomed.

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.710
- Everyone had given up.
- It can't be, It can't be.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:28.780
But Dad didn't give up.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.080
I beg you...

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.980
Please... Somehow please...

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:35.180
Please save Romeo...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.780
Somehow, please...

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.780
Dad continued pleading all night

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:42.280
with no sleep at all.

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.980
Someone who'd never set foot before in a church

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.880
prayed for the first time.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.480
And his prayers were answered.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.480
Roberto!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:08.780
Roberto!

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:11.580
The fever...

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.580
Has it gone down?

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.280
Oh, God!

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:37.980
Dad wanted to do something special to offer thanks.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.380
He worked his hardest and saved his money little by little...

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.680
and two years ago he gave his True Heart.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.080
True Heart?

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.080
Yes.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.780
Dad gave that stained glass in offering.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.280
Dad did that?

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.180
Yes, this is Roberto's True Heart.

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.580
Your own dad's True Heart.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:10.880
My dad?

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:12.580
Yes, thats right.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.580
Let me make this clear.

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.480
I won't sell Romeo.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.980
Now I'll ask you to leave.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.080
You want the thirty francs.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.880
Your only sensible choice.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:46.280
Tomorrow... no... the day after tomorrow

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.580
you'll surely sell him

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.880
to go on living.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.980
No matter what happens,

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.180
I'm not letting go of him.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.580
Romeo is my son!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.880
Remember this then

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.980
I'll be the one with the last laugh.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.680
Romeo!

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.780
I'm sorry... Dad.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.280
Why's this... you're already apologizing?

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:36.280
Such a baby...

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.580
Now now, no crying...

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.280
I'm not crying!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.080
Thank goodness...

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:46.980
Truly, thank goodness.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:49.980
Where's that guy?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.580
Has he already left?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.980
All right, let's start over from today, everyone.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.280
Start over?

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:17.480
Starting over from this point having lost everything.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.480
Our family's great first step.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.780
Yeah.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.980
Sure, why not?

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.780
Even without money things will surely work out

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.880
as long as the family is togather.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:32.780
Dad?

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.180
Romeo!

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.180
Dad!

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.180
Roberto!

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.580
Dad!

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:55.580
I've decided to go to Milan and clean chimneys.

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:59.880
I'm not going to give in!

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:03.580
I'm... I'm... I'm Dad's kid!

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:07.580
Next time: Farewell, My Village. See you next time!

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:14.570
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:23.270 --> 00:22:27.370
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:27.470 --> 00:22:31.670
seem to end so soon?

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:35.870
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:40.070
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:44.980
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.880
Once again in the sky

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:56.180
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:01.780
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:05.980
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
